================================================================================
Bundled third-party model weights
================================================================================

Separately from this project's own weights (documented above), the packaged
application bundles pretrained text-recognition models so it runs offline:

  craft_mlt_25k.pth (text detection) ........ ~80 MB, distributed by JaidedAI/EasyOCR
  english_g2.pth (text recognition) ......... ~14 MB, distributed by JaidedAI/EasyOCR
  docTR DBNet + PARSeq weights .............. ~190 MB, from mindee/doctr

EasyOCR itself is Apache-2.0 and publishes both of its weights from its own
releases. The detection weights are CRAFT, from NAVER Corp's
clovaai/CRAFT-pytorch — MIT-licensed, with no research-only or non-commercial
restriction on the trained model. MIT requires its copyright notice to travel
with redistributed copies:

    CRAFT: Character Region Awareness for Text Detection
    Copyright (c) 2019-present NAVER Corp.
    Licensed under the MIT License; see https://github.com/clovaai/CRAFT-pytorch

The docTR checkpoints are Apache-2.0, matching the docTR project itself.

The EasyOCR and docTR license texts are in the bundled THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt.
A source checkout bundles neither weight set: EasyOCR downloads its own on
first use, and the docTR models are fetched on demand
(vodparse.cli.doctr_support fetch).


================================================================================
Optional GPU acceleration (not bundled)
================================================================================

On Windows, the application can download NVIDIA CUDA builds of PyTorch, but
only after an explicit user request (File ▸ GPU Acceleration). Those wheels
include NVIDIA proprietary components, are fetched directly from their
publisher at the user's initiative, and are governed by NVIDIA's own license
terms. They are not redistributed as part of this project, and no shipped
build contains them.
